* CUSTOMER MASTER UPDATE
*
* Keyed VSAM update driven by a transaction file, with an instream lookup
* table, a CASE, a called audit program and a file EXIT.  Between them they
* cover the things a field lineage has to be honest about:
*
*   POINT selects WHICH record is read - a dependency of a different kind
*     from a value flowing into a field, and reported as such.
*   SEARCH returns the table's description; the argument decides the row.
*   CALL is opaque - its arguments may come back changed.
*   EXIT(TRANEDIT) sees every TRANS record before this program does.
*
FILE TRANS FB(120 1200) EXIT(TRANEDIT)
  TR-CUST         1   9 N
  TR-CODE        10   1 A
  TR-AMT         11   5 P 2
  TR-DATE        16   8 N
*
FILE CUSTMAST VS UPDATE
  CM-CUST         1   9 N
  CM-BAL         10   5 P 2
  CM-LAST        15   8 N
  CM-STAT        23   1 A
*
FILE ERRLOG FB(133 1330) PRINTER
  ER-TEXT         1 132 A
*
FILE CODETAB TABLE INSTREAM
  CT-CODE         1   1 A
  CT-DESC         3  20 A
'D' DEPOSIT
'W' WITHDRAWAL
ENDTABLE
*
DEFINE WS-NEWBAL   W  5 P 2
DEFINE WS-DESC     W 20 A
DEFINE WS-MSG      W 132 A
DEFINE WS-COUNT    W  4 P 0
*
JOB INPUT TRANS NAME UPDJOB FINISH WRAPUP
  SEARCH CODETAB WITH TR-CODE GIVING WS-DESC
  POINT CUSTMAST EQ TR-CUST
  GET CUSTMAST
  CASE TR-CODE
    WHEN 'D'
      WS-NEWBAL = CM-BAL + TR-AMT
    WHEN 'W'
      WS-NEWBAL = CM-BAL - TR-AMT
    OTHERWISE
      PERFORM BAD-CODE
  END-CASE
  CM-BAL  = WS-NEWBAL
  CM-LAST = TR-DATE
  WRITE CUSTMAST UPDATE
  WS-COUNT = WS-COUNT + 1
*
BAD-CODE. PROC
  WS-MSG = WS-DESC
  MOVE WS-MSG TO ER-TEXT
  PUT ERRLOG
  CALL AUDITLOG USING (TR-CUST TR-CODE TR-AMT)
END-PROC
*
WRAPUP. PROC
  DISPLAY 'CUSTOMERS UPDATED: ' WS-COUNT
END-PROC
